From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@localhost>
Date: Sat Oct 31 12:30:00 2026 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pci: sky1-cix: avoid NULL dereference when no endpoint bus exists

sky1_pcie_get_ep_pci_dev() is reached from the PME work item and from
both AER interrupt paths.  It walks bridge->bus->children and then
root_bus->devices without checking either pointer.

The host bridge's root bus is not populated until the link is up, and
the function is also called from paths that can run while the link is
down or the endpoint has been removed (PME wake, AER storm on a failed
link).  A NULL bridge->bus or the absence of any child bus makes the
walk dereference NULL.

Bail out with NULL before each walk when the required bus object does
not exist; callers already handle a NULL endpoint.

Signed-off-by: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@localhost>
---
 0178-pci-sky1-cix-guard-ep-lookup-against-missing-bus.patch | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pci-sky1-cix.c
@@ -309,12 +309,19 @@
 	if (!bridge)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/* The root bus may not exist yet while the link is still down. */
+	if (!bridge->bus)
+		return NULL;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(child, &bridge->bus->children, node) {
 		if (child->parent == bridge->bus) {
 			root_bus = child;
 			break;
 		}
 	}
+
+	if (!root_bus)
+		return NULL;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(pdev, &root_bus->devices, bus_list) {
 		if (PCI_SLOT(pdev->devfn) == 0) {
